{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"CLSA-2026-1789565568","published":"2026-09-16T13:32:59Z","modified":"2026-10-26T09:32:02.220465006Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-86421"],"summary":"Fix CVE(s): CVE-2026-86421","details":"   * SECURITY UPDATE: memory leak in the MSL group handler\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-86421.patch: destroy the per-level DrawInfo in\n       the </group> unwind of MSLEndElement. The unwind released the image,\n       the attributes and the image_info of every level it popped, but never\n       the DrawInfo that MSLPushImage clones for that level, so each nested\n       <group> element leaked one DrawInfo (coders/msl.c)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-86421-1.patch: bound that unwind loop so a\n       stale group_info numImages count cannot drive msl_info->n below zero.\n       This version predates upstream 8867bada, so the loop had no bound and\n       the DrawInfo destroy added above would otherwise widen the existing\n       out-of-bounds free by one pointer (coders/msl.c)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-86421-2.patch: destroy the per-level DrawInfo\n       in MSLPopImage() too. MSLPopImage handles the </image> pop outside a\n       group and is disjoint from the </group> unwind patched above; this\n       version predates upstream 08278c7c (first released in 6.9.10-0), so\n       without it a crafted MSL document repeating <image>...</image> still\n       leaks one DrawInfo per pop (coders/msl.c)\n     - CVE-2026-86421","affected":[{"package":{"name":"imagemagick","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:16.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/imagemagick?distro=ubuntu-16.04"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8:6.8.9.9-7ubuntu5.17+tuxcare.els59"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/ubuntu16.04els/CLSA-2026-1789565568.json"}},{"package":{"name":"imagemagick-6.q16","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:16.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/imagemagick-6.q16?distro=ubuntu-16.04"},"ranges":[{"